<spell-notebook "label theming">
	<header level="1">
		Label
		<header>A label displays content classification.</>
	</>
	<label-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-label-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a `<ui-labels>` group,
			`:root`), or on the label's box through `::part(label)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads
			each through a private alias, so nothing inside blocks them.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* square tags in one group */
			ui-labels.tags {
			  --ui-label-radius: 0;
			}
			/* an owner of yours, with a 2px border */
			.photo-frame {
			  position: relative;
			  --ui-label-owner-edge: 2px;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				Positioned labels (`corner`, `ribbon`, `attached`, `floating`) read `--ui-label-owner-edge` and
				`--ui-label-owner-radius` from their owner, so set those on the element that holds them (`<ui-segment>`,
				`<ui-input>` ... set them for you). Never set the `--_ui-label-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-label" playground>
				<ui-label icon="envelope">23</>
				<ui-text paragraph><kbd><ui-label>Ctrl</></> + <kbd><ui-label>Alt</></> + <kbd><ui-label>Del</></> <kbd><ui-label appearance="basic">W</></><kbd><ui-label appearance="basic">A</></><kbd><ui-label appearance="basic">S</></></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
